# Normalize line endings to LF regardless of the checkout platform or the
# cloning user's local `core.autocrlf` setting. Without this, Windows users
# who clone with Git's own default (`core.autocrlf=true`) get CRLF line
# endings in every text file, which can break parsers that assume LF or
# anchor regexes on end-of-line. This file is the first line of defense;
# the second is that scripts/lint-designkit.mjs normalizes `\r\n` -> `\n`
# after reading, as defense in depth.
* text=auto eol=lf
